- Hash map + pick top-2: O(n) time, O(m) extra space (m distinct elements). Exactly returns the two most frequent elements.
- Boyer–Moore generalized (n/3): O(n) time, O(1) extra space, but only finds elements whose frequency > n/3 (at most two). If you need the absolute top-2 by frequency regardless of threshold, use the hash-map approach.

